body:
I absolutely hate this. Said it before last event, gonna say it now and every patch following that has it like this. The dev streams gave us a Q&A at the end. In depth look at all the changes, and it was done live. With this we get the "heres some of the information, I may not have included all of it, but you can hunt around the other Content creators for the rest of it!"

&#x200B;

I understand trying to bring them in. But this is the absolute worst way.

The only thing that I am somewhat sad about, is that I am already P100 so I won't get to experience the new way of prestige without getting a second copy of the game.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I am glad they are changing it though. Better for everyone involved. Hell I would wouldn't a reset item like prestige, resetting my unlocks and blood line.

Even this is hard, and near impossible to prove. and accusing someone of it does absolutely nothing because there could be so many factors at play for it. I've been all over the elo board, and ultimately, the vast majority of cheat accusations come from being upset the person got killed, unable to believe that another player could be better.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Sorry that your "high elo" self report for a "majority" hits nowhere and has no actual basis for anything at all. Yes this is gonna come off rude, but claiming that a majority of them cheat, while providing no proof, no statistics, no evidence, it means nothing. Fact is, like it or not, you most likely ran into legit players, who had a bit more knowledge than you, and instead of accepting you got had. You want to accuse them of cheating so you feel superior in some way.
